# Ford Popular 103E two-door saloon, 1953-1959.
#
# The sidevalve Popular on the old E494A Anglia shell: 3,848 mm long, 1,435 mm
# wide, 1,638 mm high, 2,286 mm wheelbase (The Motor road test, 1954); 1,172 cc
# sidevalve four, three-speed gearbox, vacuum wiper.
# Britain's cheapest new car of the mid-1950s and a huge 1950s-60s parc.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Popular
#
# Colours: Black, Grey, Blue and Green are documented Ford colours of the period.
#
# Weight: 220 in total (black 80, grey 55, blue 45, green 40), the entry-level car
# of its decade.
#
# Speed 100 km/h; comfort 35/383 (line). Classes 1,2.
# Dates: 1953-1959 with a road tail to about 1972.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-popular-103e.blend. References:
# citycars/references/ford-popular-103e/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

